s and pancytopenia", "Aplastic anemia with pancytopenia: less likely due to presence of blasts and elevated WBC"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Pancytopenia with blasts", "Unexplained visual decline"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.002, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.28085110880780295, "posterior": 0.24549284170890098, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) is rare in adults and typically presents with lymphoid-specific markers. The absence of these and the patient’s age make ALL…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Plasma Cell Disorder", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.10638301756906465, "posterior": 0.025521262353180207, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The lack of these hallmark features for plasma cell disorders (e.g., multiple myeloma) strongly argues against this diagnosis."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label